related_terms.medium_def:
The Deity; 
called LORD or LORD (KJV= Jehovah) (יהוה); or LORD (KJV= Jehovah) (יְהֹוִה); or LORD (יָהּ); or Lord (אֲדֹנָי); or God (KJV= Elohim) (אֱלֹהִים); or Baal (KJV= Baali; NIV= Master) (בַּעֲלִי); or Almighty (שַׁדַּי); or Most High (עַל); or Most High (Aramiac עִלַּי); or Most High (KJV= "most High") or Most High (KJV= Highest) (עֶלְיוֹן); or Most High (Aramiac עֶלְיוֹן); or God/ Most High (KJV= "most high God") (אֵל עֶלְיוֹן); or God (אֵל=God); or El/-Elohe (אֵל אֱלֹהִים); or El/-Elohe Israel (=Alt tag) (אֵל אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל); or Banner (KJV= Nissi) (נֵס); or Banner (KJV= Nissi) (=Alt tag) (יְהֹוָה נִסִּי); or Peace (KJV= Shalom) (שָׁלוֹם); or Peace (KJV= Shalom) (=Alt tag) (יְהֹוָה שָׁלוֹם); or Provider (KJV= Jireh) (יִרְאֶה); or Provider (KJV= Jireh) (=Alt tag) (יִרְאֶה); or LORD our Righteousness (NIV= Righteous Saviour) (צִדְקֵנוּ); or LORD our Righteousness (NIV= Righteous Saviour) (יְהֹוָה צִדְקֵנוּ (=Alt tag)); or Everlasting (NIV= Eternal) (עוֹלָם); or Jealous (קַנָּא); or Hosts (NIV= Almighty) (צָבָא); or Highest (ὕψιστος); or "hosts" (KJV= "sabaoth;" NIV= Almighty) (σαβαώθ); or Abba (ἀββά); or Eli (ἠλί); or Eloi (ἐλωΐ) §Shaddai, the Almighty (God) 
This name means almighty, most powerful

A High Priest living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Sa.1.3; 
only referred to as Eli (עֵלִי); 
father of Hophni, Phinehas. § descendant of Aaron through Ithamar and high priest and judge of Israel when Samuel entered service as a child

A location first mentioned at Num.34.4; 
only referred to as Akrabbim (עַקְרַבִּים). § a pass on the southern border of Palestine
scorpion-pass; ascent of Akrabbim

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.36.23; 
referred to as Alvan or Alvan (עַלְיָן, עַלְוָן); 
son of Shobal; 
a brother of Manahath, Ebal, Shepho and Onam. § a Horite, son of Shobal

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.25.26; 
referred to as Israel or [ ] or Israelite or "God" (KJV= Israel) (יִשְׂרָאֵל), or Israel (Aramiac יִשְׂרָאֵל), or Jacob or "he" (KJV= Jacob) (יַעֲקֹב), or Jeshurun (יְשֻׁרוּן), or Israelite (יִשְׂרְאֵלִי), or Israelitess (יִשְׂרְאֵלִית), or Israel or Israelite (Ἰσραήλ), or Jacob (Ἰακώβ), or Israelite or Israel (Ἰσραηλίτης); 
son of Isaac and Rebekah; 
a brother of Esau; 
husband of Rachel, Leah, Zilpah and Bilhah; 
father of Reuben, Simeon, Levi, Judah, Dan, Naphtali, Gad, Asher, Issachar, Zebulun, Dinah, Joseph and Benjamin. § son of Isaac, grandson of Abraham, and father of the 12 patriarchs of the tribes of Israel

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.3.24; 
only referred to as Akkub (עַקּוּב); 
son of Elioenai; 
a brother of Hodaviah, Eliashib, Pelaiah, Johanan, Delaiah and Anani.
